  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've just put in a new lever-style kitchen faucet only to find it's leaking! Often, it comes down to a few common installation mishaps. Did you use sealant or a gasket as directed? Sometimes, a tiny bit of water can sneak through if that seal isn't just right. Another frequent culprit is overtightening the supply line connections, which can actually damage the washers or crimp lines, leading to a drip. Or maybe the opposite happened and they're just not tight enough! It's a delicate balance. Before you panic, shut off the water supply and double-check those connections underneath the sink. Make sure everything feels snug but not strained. If you're still scratching your head, or if you've got older plumbing that seems to be contributing to the problem, that's when it's smart to call in a pro. Here at HH Remodeling LLC, we've seen it all and can quickly diagnose and fix those persistent leaks, ensuring your new faucet works perfectly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}